$f(3) = 0.375$.
$f(4) = 0.25$.
Since $f(x)$ is strictly decreasing for $x \ge 2$, if $a_i, a_j \ge 2$ and $a_i \neq a_j$, then $f(a_i) \neq f(a_j)$.
